{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N1"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 121, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A residual shortcut to the output helps when a conv path exists on edge 4 but hurts parameter-free cells where edge 4 is skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In pooling-dominated cells, turning edge 3 into identity removes or dilutes the only useful signal path, causing large drops."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling with a 3x3 conv adds the key learnable capacity to otherwise weak cells, giving very large gains."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 is none, node 1 is zero, so a conv on edge 1->3 processes nothing and the edit is nearly useless."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In cells that already have convs, replacing the skip shortcut with a conv removes the residual path and hurts, while in conv-free cells it helps greatly."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct 0->3 edge, cutting edge 0 can disconnect the output from the input, collapsing accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, removing edge 5 leaves only edge 3 into the output, which can disconnect it and is catastrophic."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is missing, edge 3 is one of few routes to the output, so deleting it is far more damaging."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with a 1x1 loses capacity, whereas replacing skip, pool, or none adds capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a learned 3x3 conv into the output for identity hurts, while swapping none or pool for skip is neutral to positive."}], "tok": 18052, "bad": 1, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_